BAR Droid phone version of BAR's Defense Range GL4 (luaui/widgets/gui_defenserange_gl4.lua): the same rings with fewer
points. Every ring point fits the ring to the ground with a heightmap search in the vertex shader, for every ring of every
defence in view, in three passes: 64 points a ring instead of 128 (nukes and long-range cannons 256, not 1024) and 6
search steps instead of 8 (a ring's edge within 1/64 of its range, the heightmap's grid is 8 elmos); mobile anti-nukes'
rings follow their units every 3rd frame. Its GPU time was the costliest widget's on the dev phone in a late 16-player game
(docs/ENGINE-SIM.md on engine/sim, "BAR's Lua on phones"). Applied by the engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir) to BAR's file as
LuaUI loads it; if a block finds no place, BAR's own file runs.

@@@ find
local largeCircleSegments = 1024
@@@ with
local largeCircleSegments = 256 -- BAR Droid (phone): 1024
@@@ end

@@@ find
local smallCircleSegments = 128
@@@ with
local smallCircleSegments = 64 -- BAR Droid (phone): 128
@@@ end

@@@ find
local rangeHeightmapSampleSteps = 8
@@@ with
local rangeHeightmapSampleSteps = 6 -- BAR Droid (phone): 8
@@@ end

@@@ find
local antiupdaterate = 1
@@@ with
local antiupdaterate = 3 -- BAR Droid (phone): 1
@@@ end
